  "title": "Armenia adopts Christianity (traditional date 301)",
  "summary": "According to tradition, King Tiridates III of Armenia was healed by Gregory the Illuminator in 301 and made Christianity the national religion, making Armenia the first nation to convert. The Armenian church's seat lies at Vagharshapat (Etchmiadzin). Modern historians prefer about 314 for the official adoption, and Encyclopedia.com gives about 302 for the king's baptism.",
